Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) upon the creator of
an original work of authorship at the moment of creation, without requiring
any formality or registration.

Certain creators wish to permanently relinquish those rights to contribute
their works to a commons that the public can reliably build upon, modify,
and redistribute without fear of legal claims. Such contributions may be
motivated by ideals of free culture, scientific progress, or other personal,
philosophical, or strategic reasons.

The person applying this document to a Work (the "Affirmer") chooses to do
so while preserving their anonymity, exercising the internationally
recognized right to anonymous expression. The Affirmer, to the extent that
they hold Copyright and Related Rights in the Work, voluntarily elects to
apply this document with full knowledge of its intended legal effect.

The Affirmer understands and intends that this Waiver and License shall
remain effective regardless of whether the Affirmer's identity is later
revealed, voluntarily or involuntarily. The act of applying this document
constitutes an irrevocable commitment to the terms stated herein.


Limitations on Scope of Authority

This Waiver and License extend solely to rights that the Affirmer lawfully
possesses. No provision of this document shall be construed as:

  a. authorizing the disclosure of information subject to legal duties of
     confidentiality;
  b. immunizing any person from criminal liability under applicable law;
  c. affecting the rights of third parties in materials that may be
     incorporated in the Work;
  d. waiving, restricting, or otherwise affecting any right of any third
     party that is not a party to this document;
  e. creating any obligation on persons who are not parties to this
     document; or
  f. constituting an admission by the Affirmer regarding the lawfulness,
     origin, or ownership of the Work.

Persons who access, use, or redistribute the Work bear sole responsibility
for ensuring compliance with all applicable laws and third-party rights.

1. Definitions.

  a. Affirmer

     The natural person or legal entity that applies this document to a Work
     and that chooses to remain anonymous or pseudonymous. The Affirmer
     represents that, to the best of the Affirmer's knowledge, the Affirmer
     holds Copyright and Related Rights in the Work sufficient to grant the
     Waiver and License herein.

     Where the Affirmer is a legal entity, references to actions, rights,
     or obligations of the Affirmer shall be understood to apply to the
     entity acting through its authorized representatives.

  b. AI-Generated Output

     Any content produced by a Machine Learning Model during inference or
     deployment, including but not limited to text, code, images, audio,
     video, or other media, regardless of the degree of human involvement
     in the generation process.

  c. Applicable Law

     The body of legal rules, whether statutory, customary, treaty-based,
     or derived from judicial precedent, that governs the validity,
     interpretation, and effect of this document in a particular geographic
     territory or legal system at the time of application or enforcement.

  d. Copyright and Related Rights

     All exclusive rights arising under Applicable Law with respect to the
     Work, including but not limited to:

       i. the right to reproduce, adapt, distribute, perform, display,
          communicate, and translate the Work;
      ii. neighboring rights, sui generis rights, and related rights,
          including but not limited to performers' rights, phonogram
          producers' rights, broadcasters' rights, and film producers'
          rights;
     iii. rights protecting the extraction, dissemination, use, and reuse
          of data in the Work;
      iv. database rights (sui generis database rights), including those
          arising under Directive 96/9/EC of the European Parliament and
          of the Council and any national implementations or successor
          legislation thereof;
       v. rights protecting against unfair competition to the extent such
          rights are based on or analogous to copyright interests in the
          Work, but excluding trademark rights and patent rights;
      vi. any other similar, equivalent, or corresponding rights throughout
          the world based on Applicable Law or treaty, whether currently
          existing or hereafter created.

  e. Covenant Not to Sue

     An irrevocable promise by the Affirmer not to initiate or maintain
     legal proceedings, assert claims, or seek remedies against any person
     based on specified grounds, even if the underlying rights cannot be
     waived under Applicable Law. This covenant runs with the Work and
     binds the Affirmer and the Affirmer's Successors.

  f. Digital Trace

     Any information pattern extractable from the Work or its distribution
     that could potentially be used to identify or infer the Affirmer's
     identity, including but not limited to:

       i. coding style characteristics, programming paradigms, or
          architectural patterns;
      ii. linguistic patterns, vocabulary choices, or stylistic markers in
          comments or documentation;
     iii. choice of algorithms, libraries, dependencies, or toolchains;
      iv. temporal patterns of creation, modification, or distribution; or
       v. any combination of the above that, when analyzed collectively,
          could serve as a unique behavioral or technical signature.

  g. Fallback License

     A conditional grant of permission that automatically becomes effective
     if and to the extent the Waiver is determined to be legally invalid,
     unenforceable, or ineffective under Applicable Law in any
     jurisdiction.

  h. Identifiable Information

     Any data or combination of data that could reasonably be used, either
     alone or in conjunction with other available information, to ascertain
     the identity, location, contact details, or other personal
     characteristics of the Affirmer, including but not limited to:

       i. legal names, birth names, or aliases;
      ii. persistent pseudonyms used across multiple contexts;
     iii. biometric data or unique physiological characteristics;
      iv. network identifiers, IP addresses, or device fingerprints;
       v. financial account information or transaction records; or
      vi. any combination of Metadata or Digital Traces that collectively
          enable identification.

  i. Jurisdictional Severability

     The principle that the validity and enforceability of each provision
     of this document shall be determined independently under each body of
     Applicable Law, such that:

       i. a determination of invalidity in one jurisdiction does not affect
          validity in other jurisdictions; and
      ii. the invalidity of one provision in a jurisdiction does not affect
          the validity of other provisions in that jurisdiction, unless
          such provisions are inseverable.

  j. Machine Learning Model

     Any computational system, process, or method that generates outputs
     based on patterns extracted from input data, regardless of the
     underlying technical methodology, including but not limited to:

       i. artificial neural networks and deep learning systems;
      ii. statistical models and probabilistic inference systems;
     iii. symbolic AI and rule-based systems trained on data;
      iv. hybrid systems combining multiple approaches; or
       v. any future technology serving a similar functional purpose.

  k. Metadata

     Descriptive, technical, administrative, or structural data embedded
     in, attached to, or otherwise associated with the Work, including but
     not limited to:

       i. file creation, modification, and access timestamps;
      ii. software version information, compiler details, or build
          environment data;
     iii. version control system records (commit hashes, commit messages,
          author fields, branch names);
      iv. geolocation data, time zone information, or locale settings;
       v. device identifiers, operating system fingerprints, or hardware
          signatures;
      vi. network protocol headers, transmission metadata, or routing
          information; or
     vii. digital signatures, cryptographic key fingerprints, or hash
          values.

  l. Moral Rights

     Rights that are deemed in certain jurisdictions to be personal to or
     inseparable from the author, including but not limited to:

       i. the right to be identified as the author (right of attribution,
          paternity, or authorship);
      ii. the right to object to derogatory treatment, distortion, or
          mutilation of the Work (right of integrity);
     iii. the right to control first publication or disclosure (right of
          disclosure or divulgation);
      iv. the right to withdraw the Work from circulation (right of
          withdrawal or retraction); or
       v. any similar personal rights recognized under Applicable Law,
          whether denominated as "moral rights", "droit moral", or
          otherwise.

  m. Public Domain

     The status of a work that is not subject to any person's exclusive
     Copyright and Related Rights under Applicable Law and may be freely
     used, modified, and distributed by any person without permission,
     attribution, or payment.

     For purposes of this document, a work is in the Public Domain in a
     given jurisdiction if no Copyright and Related Rights subsist in that
     work under the laws of that jurisdiction.

  n. Successor

     Any natural person or legal entity that acquires the Affirmer's
     Copyright and Related Rights in the Work through:

       i. inheritance or intestate succession;
      ii. testamentary disposition or bequest;
     iii. operation of law (including bankruptcy, dissolution, or judicial
          decree);
      iv. contractual transfer or assignment (whether voluntary or
          involuntary); or
       v. any other means recognized under Applicable Law.

  o. Termination Rights

     Any right, whether arising from statute, regulation, judicial
     precedent, treaty obligation, or public policy, that would permit the
     Affirmer, Successors, or any other person to:

       i. revoke, rescind, cancel, or terminate this Waiver or License;
      ii. renegotiate the terms of this document;
     iii. recapture or reclaim rights granted herein; or
      iv. challenge the effectiveness of this document after a specified
          period of time or upon specified conditions,

     including but not limited to rights under 17 U.S.C. § 203 (United
     States), the copyright term extension provisions of various
     jurisdictions, or similar statutory provisions worldwide.

  p. Training Data

     Any collection, compilation, corpus, or dataset of works used to
     train, fine-tune, validate, test, or otherwise develop a Machine
     Learning Model, regardless of:

       i. format, organization, or storage medium;
      ii. whether the data is used in its original form or preprocessed;
     iii. whether the data is retained after training or discarded; or
      iv. the specific training methodology or algorithm employed.

  q. Waiver

     A unilateral, voluntary, and irrevocable act by which the Affirmer
     permanently relinquishes, abandons, and surrenders Copyright and
     Related Rights in the Work to the fullest extent permitted by
     Applicable Law, with the express intent of dedicating the Work to the
     Public Domain for the benefit of the public.

  r. Work

     The specific copyrightable work of authorship, fixed in any tangible
     medium of expression, to which the Affirmer has applied this document,
     including but not limited to:

       i. literary works (including source code, object code, and
          documentation);
      ii. artistic works (including visual art, photographs, and graphic
          designs);
     iii. musical works and sound recordings;
      iv. audiovisual works (including films, videos, and animations);
       v. databases and compilations;
      vi. architectural works; or
     vii. any derivative works, compiled forms, or translations thereof
          created by the Affirmer.


2. Copyright and Related Rights.

A Work made available under this document may be protected by Copyright and
Related Rights under Applicable Law. For purposes of this document,
Copyright and Related Rights are defined comprehensively in Section 1(d)
and include all rights specified therein, whether currently recognized or
hereafter created under Applicable Law.


3. Waiver.

To the greatest extent permitted by, but not in contravention of, Applicable
Law, the Affirmer hereby overtly, fully, permanently, irrevocably, and
unconditionally waives, abandons, and surrenders all of the Affirmer's
Copyright and Related Rights and associated claims and causes of action,
whether now known or unknown (including existing as well as future claims
and causes of action), in the Work:

  a. in all territories worldwide, including territories where copyright
     protection may be established in the future;
  b. for the maximum duration provided by Applicable Law, including any
     extensions to the term of protection whether currently enacted or
     hereafter established;
  c. in any current or future medium and for any number of copies; and
  d. for any purpose whatsoever, including without limitation commercial,
     advertising, promotional, educational, research, or private purposes

(the "Waiver"). The Affirmer makes the Waiver for the benefit of each
member of the public at large and to the detriment of the Affirmer's heirs
and Successors, fully intending that such Waiver shall not be subject to
revocation, rescission, cancellation, termination, or any other legal or
equitable action to disrupt the quiet enjoyment of the Work by the public
as contemplated by the Affirmer's express Statement of Purpose.

The Affirmer understands that the Waiver may not be fully effective in all
jurisdictions due to variations in Applicable Law, particularly in
jurisdictions that do not recognize the concept of Public Domain dedication
or that impose mandatory copyright protection. In such jurisdictions, the
Fallback License in Section 4 shall apply.

To the extent permitted by Applicable Law, the Affirmer waives any and all
Termination Rights that may arise, including any statutory or equitable
right to reclaim or renegotiate the terms of this Waiver after any period
of time. The Affirmer acknowledges that in certain jurisdictions,
Termination Rights may be inalienable and therefore this waiver of
Termination Rights may be ineffective; in such cases, the Affirmer hereby
covenants not to exercise such Termination Rights contrary to the Statement
of Purpose.

This Waiver shall remain effective regardless of whether the Affirmer's
identity is subsequently revealed, whether voluntarily or through legal
compulsion, technical analysis, or any other means.


4. Public License Fallback.

Should any part of the Waiver for any reason be judged legally invalid,
unenforceable, or ineffective under Applicable Law, then the Waiver shall
be preserved to the maximum extent permitted taking into account the
Affirmer's express Statement of Purpose. To the extent the Waiver is not
fully effective, the following license shall automatically apply:

The Affirmer hereby grants to each affected person a royalty-free,
transferable, sublicensable, non-exclusive, irrevocable, and unconditional
license to exercise the Affirmer's Copyright and Related Rights in the
Work:

  a. in all territories worldwide;
  b. for the maximum duration provided by Applicable Law, including any
     extensions to the term of protection;
  c. in any current or future medium and for any number of copies; and
  d. for any purpose whatsoever, including without limitation commercial,
     advertising, promotional, educational, research, or private purposes

(the "License"). The License shall be deemed effective as of the date this
document was applied by the Affirmer to the Work.

Should any part of the License for any reason be judged legally invalid or
ineffective under Applicable Law, such partial invalidity or ineffectiveness
shall not invalidate the remainder of the License, and in such case the
Affirmer hereby affirms that the Affirmer will not:

  a. exercise any of the Affirmer's remaining Copyright and Related Rights
     in the Work; or

  b. assert any associated claims and causes of action with respect to the
     Work,

in either case contrary to the Affirmer's express Statement of Purpose.

The Affirmer acknowledges that this commitment may not be legally
enforceable in all jurisdictions, but nevertheless declares this to be the
Affirmer's true intent.


5. Moral Rights and Attribution.

  a. Waiver of Moral Rights.

     To the greatest extent permitted by Applicable Law, the Affirmer
     waives and agrees not to assert any Moral Rights held by the Affirmer
     in the Work.

     JURISDICTIONAL NOTICE: In certain jurisdictions, particularly those
     following the civil law tradition (including but not limited to
     France, Germany, Italy, Spain, Japan, and other jurisdictions that
     have implemented Article 6bis of the Berne Convention for the
     Protection of Literary and Artistic Works), Moral Rights are deemed
     to be inalienable personal rights that cannot be waived or
     transferred. In such jurisdictions, the waiver set forth in this
     Section 5(a) shall be of no force or effect, and the Covenant Not to
     Sue in Section 5(b) shall apply instead.

  b. Covenant Not to Sue for Moral Rights.

     Where waiver of Moral Rights is prohibited, restricted, or otherwise
     ineffective under Applicable Law, the Affirmer hereby makes an
     irrevocable, unconditional, and worldwide Covenant Not to Sue any
     person for:

       i. exercising rights in the Work without providing attribution,
          credit, or acknowledgment to the Affirmer;
      ii. failing to identify the Affirmer as the author or creator of the
          Work in any manner;
     iii. modifying, adapting, translating, or creating derivative works
          based on the Work;
      iv. treating the Work in any manner that the Affirmer might otherwise
          claim to be derogatory, prejudicial to honor or reputation, or a
          distortion or mutilation of the Work;
       v. associating the Work with any product, service, cause, or
          institution, or using the Work in any context that the Affirmer
          might find objectionable; or
      vi. any other act or omission that would otherwise constitute a
          violation of Moral Rights under Applicable Law.

     This Covenant Not to Sue extends to the Affirmer's Successors and
     binds them to the same extent as it binds the Affirmer.

  c. Attribution Exemption.

     No person who exercises rights in the Work under this document is
     required or expected to:

       i. retain, reproduce, or display any copyright notice, authorship
          attribution, or license notice in copies or derivative works;
      ii. acknowledge the Affirmer or indicate the source of the Work in
          any manner;
     iii. provide any form of credit, attribution, acknowledgment, or
          citation whatsoever; or
      iv. indicate that modifications have been made to the Work.

     Any person may, at their sole discretion, choose to provide
     attribution, but such attribution is entirely voluntary and does not
     create any obligation or expectation for others to do likewise.


6. Privacy Protection and Anonymity.

  a. Minimum Necessary Information Principle (Non-Binding Guidance).

     LEGAL NOTICE: This Section 6(a) constitutes non-binding guidance and
     ethical recommendations, not legally enforceable obligations. Nothing
     in this Section 6(a) shall be construed as creating any duty, cause
     of action, or liability on any person. Compliance with applicable
     data protection, privacy, and information security laws is governed
     exclusively by such laws and not by this document.

     As a matter of ethical practice consistent with the Statement of
     Purpose, where Applicable Law, institutional policy, or legitimate
     legal process requires the retention or disclosure of information
     about the Affirmer in connection with the use or distribution of the
     Work, the Affirmer respectfully suggests that such information be
     limited to the minimum necessary to satisfy the specific legal
     requirement.

     Examples of such requirements may include:

       i. court orders or subpoenas in criminal investigations;
      ii. anti-money laundering or counter-terrorism financing obligations;
     iii. institutional policies of academic publishers, research
          repositories, or funding agencies that mandate author
          identification; or
      iv. export control or national security regulations.

     Where any such requirement applies, the Affirmer respectfully suggests
     that the person or entity subject to the requirement consider:

       i. collecting and retaining only such Identifiable Information as
          is strictly necessary to comply with the specific legal
          obligation;
      ii. maintaining such information confidentially and protecting it
          with reasonable security measures;
     iii. refraining from publicly disclosing such information except to
          the extent required by law or judicial order; and
      iv. destroying or anonymizing such information when the legal
          requirement that justified its collection no longer applies,
          unless retention is mandated by law.

  b. Metadata and Digital Trace Handling.

     The Affirmer acknowledges that the Work may contain Metadata or
     Digital Traces that could potentially be used to identify the Affirmer
     or infer information about the Affirmer.

     The Affirmer hereby declares that:

       i. the Affirmer waives any claim based on the use of Metadata or
          Digital Traces for identification purposes, except where such use
          violates independent legal obligations (such as data protection
          laws or computer fraud statutes);
      ii. any person is authorized to remove, modify, obfuscate, or
          anonymize any Metadata or Digital Traces in the Work, and such
          actions shall not constitute a violation of any right held by the
          Affirmer, including Moral Rights; and
     iii. the Affirmer will not assert that Metadata or Digital Traces
          alone constitute sufficient evidence of authorship or ownership
          in any civil proceeding concerning the Work, except where
          necessary to defend against a fraudulent claim of authorship by a
          third party.

  c. Privacy Protection Request to Downstream Users.

     The Affirmer respectfully requests, as a matter of ethical practice
     and in the spirit of this document's Statement of Purpose, that any
     person who, through technical analysis, forensic investigation, or
     other means, obtains information that could reasonably be used to
     identify the Affirmer:

       i. refrain from publicly disclosing such Identifiable Information
          unless one of the exceptions in Section 6(d) applies; and
      ii. if storing such information for legitimate purposes, protect it
          with reasonable security measures and limit access to those with
          a genuine need to know.

     LEGAL NOTICE: This Section 6(c) constitutes a request, not a legally
     binding obligation on any person. The Affirmer acknowledges that third
     parties cannot be contractually bound by this provision absent their
     express agreement. Nevertheless, the Affirmer expresses the sincere
     hope that users of the Work will respect this request as consistent
     with the values of privacy, anonymity, and free contribution to the
     public commons.

  d. Permitted Disclosures.

     Section 6(c) does not request that persons refrain from disclosing
     Identifiable Information where:

       i. the Affirmer has voluntarily and publicly revealed the Affirmer's
          identity in connection with the Work;
      ii. disclosure is compelled by lawful judicial order, valid subpoena,
          or other mandatory legal process in a criminal investigation or
          prosecution;
     iii. disclosure is necessary to comply with legal obligations under
          anti-money laundering, counter-terrorism financing, export
          control, or similar regulatory requirements;
      iv. disclosure is necessary to defend against a legal claim brought
          by a person falsely alleging to be the Affirmer or falsely
          claiming rights in the Work;
       v. the Affirmer has provided written consent to the disclosure; or
      vi. the information has already become publicly available through
          means other than a breach of this request.

  e. No Third-Party Liability for Disclosure.

     Nothing in this Section 6 shall be construed as creating any liability,
     obligation, or cause of action against any person who discloses
     Identifiable Information, whether or not such disclosure is consistent
     with the requests in Section 6(c).

     The Affirmer expressly disclaims any intent to impose legal
     obligations on third parties and acknowledges that such persons remain
     free to act according to their own judgment and legal obligations.

  f. Irrevocability Despite Identity Revelation.

     If the Affirmer's identity becomes known through any means after the
     application of this document to the Work, such revelation shall not:

       i. invalidate or permit revocation of the Waiver or License granted
          herein;
      ii. create any obligation on persons who obtained the Work during the
          period of anonymity to cease exercising rights, to provide
          retroactive attribution, or to modify their practices in any
          way; or
     iii. entitle the Affirmer or Successors to assert any claim against
          persons who relied on the Waiver or License during the period
          when the Affirmer's identity was unknown or who continue to
          exercise rights thereafter.


7. Machine Learning and Artificial Intelligence.

  a. Permission for AI Training.

     The Waiver and License expressly extend to the use of the Work as
     Training Data for any Machine Learning Model, including without
     limitation:

       i. reproduction, storage, and preprocessing of the Work in datasets,
          databases, or other compilations;
      ii. computational analysis, pattern extraction, statistical analysis,
          and feature engineering applied to the Work;
     iii. incorporation of learned representations, patterns, weights, or
          parameters derived from the Work into model architectures; and
      iv. any other use reasonably necessary for the development, training,
          validation, testing, or deployment of Machine Learning Models.

  b. No Restrictions on AI Training.

     The Affirmer imposes no restrictions on:

       i. the purpose for which a Machine Learning Model is trained
          (including commercial, research, governmental, or personal
          purposes);
      ii. the scale or computational resources used in training;
     iii. whether the training process or resulting model is open source or
          proprietary;
      iv. whether the resulting model is distributed, offered as a service,
          or kept private; or
       v. any other aspect of the machine learning pipeline.

  c. Anti-Attribution in AI Context.

     Consistent with Section 5(c), persons or entities that use the Work as
     Training Data or incorporate it into a Machine Learning Model are not
     required to, and are affirmatively requested not to:

       i. include attribution to the Affirmer in AI-Generated Outputs;
      ii. represent in model documentation, model cards, dataset
          documentation, metadata, publicity materials, or academic
          publications that outputs are derived from or associated with a
          particular anonymous or pseudonymous author;
     iii. maintain records linking the Work to Identifiable Information
          about the Affirmer in publicly accessible dataset documentation,
          version control systems, or data provenance tracking systems; or
      iv. use the Work in training data in a manner that would facilitate
          model inversion, membership inference, or other techniques
          designed to extract information about the Affirmer from the
          trained model.

     However, persons remain free to disclose the use of anonymous works
     generally in their training data without identifying the specific
     Affirmer.

  d. Waiver of Rights in AI-Generated Output.

     To the extent that any AI-Generated Output might be deemed under
     Applicable Law to be:

       i. a derivative work of the Work;
      ii. a reproduction or adaptation of the Work; or
     iii. otherwise subject to Copyright and Related Rights held by the
          Affirmer in the Work,

     the Affirmer waives any claim to Copyright and Related Rights in such
     output and covenants not to assert that such output infringes any
     right held by the Affirmer.

     This waiver and covenant extend to AI-Generated Outputs regardless of:

       i. the degree of similarity to the Work;
      ii. whether the output would be considered a substantial reproduction
          under Applicable Law;
     iii. whether the model was trained exclusively on the Work or on a
          dataset including the Work among many other works; or
      iv. any other factor.

  e. Limitations on AI Provisions.

     Nothing in this Section 7 shall be construed as:

       i. waiving any patent rights held by the Affirmer;
      ii. granting permission to use the Work in a manner that violates
          third-party rights or Applicable Law (such as training models for
          illegal purposes);
     iii. representing that the Work is suitable or safe for use in any
          particular machine learning application;
      iv. creating any warranty regarding the quality, accuracy, or
          characteristics of AI-Generated Outputs; or
       v. affecting the rights of persons other than the Affirmer in AI-
          Generated Outputs.


