     SOME JURISDICTIONS DO NOT ALLOW THE EXCLUSION OR LIMITATION OF
     CERTAIN CATEGORIES OF DAMAGES, OR HAVE MANDATORY RULES REGARDING
     LIABILITY FOR GROSS NEGLIGENCE, WILLFUL MISCONDUCT, FRAUD, OR
     PERSONAL INJURY. IN SUCH JURISDICTIONS, THE AFFIRMER'S LIABILITY
     SHALL BE LIMITED TO THE GREATEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW.

  d. Third-Party Rights and Lawfulness of the Work.

       i. No Warranty of Lawful Possession or Creation.

          The Affirmer makes no representation or warranty that:

          (A) the Work was lawfully created, obtained, or possessed by the
              Affirmer;
          (B) the Work does not incorporate materials, information, or code
              subject to third-party intellectual property rights, trade
              secrets, contractual restrictions, or confidentiality
              obligations;
          (C) the disclosure or use of the Work does not violate any
              criminal statute, regulatory requirement, professional duty,
              fiduciary obligation, or other legal duty; or
          (D) the Affirmer had the legal authority or right to apply this
              document to the Work.

      ii. No Authorization for Unlawful Conduct.

          This Waiver and License do not, and cannot, authorize any person
          to:

          (A) violate any legal duty of confidentiality owed to a third
              party, including obligations arising from employment
              agreements, non-disclosure agreements, attorney-client
              privilege, or other confidential relationships;
          (B) use, reproduce, or distribute information that the person
              knows or has reason to know was unlawfully obtained,
              misappropriated, or disclosed in violation of law;
          (C) engage in conduct that would constitute a criminal offense
              under Applicable Law, including but not limited to theft of
              trade secrets, unauthorized access to computer systems,
              espionage, or fraud; or
          (D) infringe the intellectual property rights or other legal
              rights of any third party.

     iii. User's Assumption of Risk and Independent Obligation.

          Any person exercising rights in the Work under this document does
          so entirely at their own risk and is solely and independently
          responsible for:

          (A) conducting due diligence and independent legal review to
              assess whether the Work may be subject to third-party rights
              or legal restrictions;
          (B) ensuring compliance with all applicable laws, regulations,
              professional standards, and ethical obligations in their
              jurisdiction and in any jurisdiction where they use or
              distribute the Work;
          (C) obtaining any necessary third-party consents, clearances,
              licenses, or authorizations before using the Work;
          (D) defending against, and bearing all costs and liabilities
              arising from, any claims, lawsuits, or regulatory actions by
              third parties alleging that the Work infringes their rights,
              violates confidentiality, or was unlawfully obtained; and
          (E) making their own independent determination of whether the
              legal and ethical risks of using the Work are acceptable.

      iv. Severability of Potentially Unlawful Content.

          If a court of competent jurisdiction or an arbitral tribunal
          determines that any portion of the Work:

          (A) was unlawfully obtained, created in violation of law, or
              subject to third-party rights that preclude the Affirmer from
              granting the Waiver or License; or
          (B) violates any legal duty or restriction,

          then such determination shall not automatically invalidate this
          document's application to the remaining portions of the Work,
          provided that:

          (A) the allegedly unlawful or infringing portion is severable
              from the remainder of the Work as a matter of fact and law;
              and
          (B) the remaining portions, standing alone, constitute
              independently copyrightable works in which the Affirmer holds
              sufficient rights to grant the Waiver and License.

          The determination of severability shall be made according to the
          Applicable Law of the jurisdiction where the claim is adjudicated,
          and a finding of non-severability in one jurisdiction shall not
          preclude a finding of severability in another jurisdiction.

       v. No Presumption of Lawfulness.

          The fact that the Work is made available under this document
          shall not be construed as evidence that:

          (A) the Work was lawfully created or obtained;
          (B) the Work does not violate third-party rights; or
          (C) use of the Work is lawful or safe.

          Each person must make their own independent assessment of these
          matters.

  e. Jurisdictional Severability and Variance.

     The validity, interpretation, and enforceability of each provision of
     this document shall be determined independently under the Applicable
     Law of each jurisdiction where the Work is used or where rights are
     exercised.

     If any provision or part of a provision is held to be invalid,
     unenforceable, or ineffective in a particular jurisdiction:

       i. such invalidity, unenforceability, or ineffectiveness shall not
          affect the validity, enforceability, or effectiveness of that
          provision in other jurisdictions; and
      ii. the remaining provisions of this document shall remain in full
          force and effect in that jurisdiction, unless such provisions are
          so interdependent that they cannot reasonably be given effect
          without the invalid provision.

     Where a provision is held invalid in a jurisdiction, it shall be
     reformed and construed in that jurisdiction to most closely effectuate
     the Affirmer's Statement of Purpose to the extent permitted by
     Applicable Law.


9. Interpretation.

  a. Entire Agreement.

     This document constitutes the entire understanding concerning the
     Waiver and License of Copyright and Related Rights in the Work and
     supersedes all prior or contemporaneous understandings, agreements,
     representations, or warranties, whether written or oral, concerning
     the subject matter of this document.

  b. Liberal Construction.

     This document shall be interpreted broadly to effectuate the
     Affirmer's Statement of Purpose of dedicating the Work to the Public
     Domain. In case of ambiguity, the interpretation that most favors the
     public's freedom to use the Work shall be preferred.

  c. No Modification or Waiver of Terms.

     This document may not be modified, amended, or supplemented by the
     Affirmer after it has been applied to the Work. Any attempt to do so
     shall be void and of no effect.

     The failure of any person to enforce any provision of this document
     shall not constitute a waiver of that provision or any other
     provision.

  d. Governing Law and Jurisdiction.

     Given the international nature of this document and its application to
     works that may be used in multiple jurisdictions simultaneously, no
     single governing law or exclusive jurisdiction is specified.

     The validity and effect of each provision shall be determined under
     the Applicable Law of the jurisdiction where rights are exercised or
     where a dispute arises, in accordance with the principle of
     Jurisdictional Severability set forth in Section 8(e).

  e. Language.

     This document is drafted in the English language. If this document is
     translated into other languages, the English version shall prevail in
     case of any conflict or discrepancy, to the extent permitted by
     Applicable Law.

  f. Headings.

     Section and subsection headings are for convenience only and shall not
     affect the interpretation of this document.

  g. Successors and Assigns.

     This document binds and benefits the Affirmer's Successors and assigns.
     The Waiver, License, and covenants herein run with the Copyright and
     Related Rights in the Work and shall remain effective regardless of
     subsequent transfers of such rights.


10. Effective Date and Term.

  a. Effective Date.

     This document takes effect immediately upon its application to the
     Work by the Affirmer. No further action, registration, or notice is
     required for this document to become effective.

  b. Term.

     The Waiver, License, and covenants in this document are perpetual and
     irrevocable. They shall remain in effect:

       i. for the entire duration of Copyright and Related Rights in the
          Work under Applicable Law; and
      ii. in perpetuity, to the extent that Applicable Law permits
          perpetual obligations.

     This document cannot be revoked, rescinded, terminated, or cancelled
     by the Affirmer or Successors, except to the extent that Applicable
     Law mandates inalienable Termination Rights that cannot be waived.
